They are the Kotlin side of the engine's JNI library, which the keyboard
downloads on request (the same release's sherpa-onnx-1.13.8.aar); the native
code finds these classes and their fields by name, so they must match that
release exactly. Changes: the loadLibrary calls are removed (the downloaded
library is loaded by path) and OnlineRecognizer.kt keeps only its classes.
